list-item.p:
State space: S is the set of possible states. For the computing capacity allocation issue at time t, the state space is the set of all PNs, S(t)={S1(t),…,Sq(t),…,SQ+1(t)}. For each PN, its state is composed of the following three parts:
(26)Sq(t)={sq(t)=(Jq(t),Dq(t),Γq(t))}
where Jq(t) represents the newly generated tasks assigned to PN q, Dq(t) represents the remaining data size of PN q, and Γq(t) represents the previous computing resource allocation of PN q.
